;; Bounded set literal, `conj`, `disj` and membership.
;;
;; Until 2026-09-03 this read
;;
;;   (if (contains? (disj (conj #{:a (+ 1 1)} :b 2) :a) :b) 1 0)
;;
;; and could not be admitted on either backend it declares. Two reasons, and
;; the fixture is the only place either had been written down:
;;
;;   1. `#{:a (+ 1 1)}` is heterogeneous, and a set literal is `[:set :keyword]`
;;      -- collections/set_heterogeneous.kotoba now pins that refusal;
;;   2. `contains?` takes a canonical `[:map K V]`; a typed set answers to
;;      `typed-set-contains`.
;;
;; `conj` and `disj` themselves had no lowering at all until the same day.
(defn main []
  (if (typed-set-contains [:set :keyword] (disj (conj #{:a} :b :c) :a) :b)
    1
    0))
